{"meta": {"title": "CGL 2026 Tier 2 Mock 9 - Hindi", "id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "total_questions": 130, "correct_score": "1", "negative_score": "1", "timer_minutes": "120", "timer_seconds": 7200}, "questions": [{"answer": "3", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50011", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">6 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">4.5 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">In △ABC, AB = 13 cm, AC = 11 cm and BC = 16 cm. If G is the centroid of the triangle, what is the length of AG?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:3pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image011.png\" width=\"271\" height=\"178\" alt ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — Apollonius: AB² + AC² = 2(AD² + BD²), where AD is the median to BC.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">D is the midpoint of BC, so BD = 16 ÷ 2 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">8 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Length of the median AD.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">13² + 11² = 2(AD² + 8²)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">169 + 121 = 2AD² + 128</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2AD² = 162 ⇒ AD² = 81 ⇒ AD = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — the centroid divides each median 2 : 1 from the vertex.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image012.png\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">6 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9 cm is the whole median and 3 cm is GD — the centroid sits two-thirds of the way down from A.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2020 Mains (Tier-II)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "2", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50012", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">25,872 cm³</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">29,106 cm³</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">16,170 cm³</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">12,936 cm³</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A solid right circular cone of base radius 21 cm is to be placed inside a long hollow cylinder of radius 35 cm so that the axis of the cone is perpendicular to the axis of the cylinder. What is the maximum possible volume of the cone? (Take π = 22/7)</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:3pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image013.png\" width=\"246\" height=\"214\" alt ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — look at the cross-section of the cylinder: a circle of radius 35 cm.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The cone's base appears as a chord of length 2 × 21 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">42 cm</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, and its apex touches the circle on the opposite side.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Distance of the base chord from the centre.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">d = √(35² − 21²) = √(1,225 − 441) = √784 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">28 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Greatest height of the cone.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">h = 35 + 28 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">63 cm</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> (centre to apex is one radius)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Volume.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">V = ⅓ × π × r² × h</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image014.png\" width=\"208\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">= 22 × 3 × 21 × 21 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">29,106 cm³</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">29,106 cm³</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Height is radius + chord distance (35 + 28), not twice the chord distance — the apex runs past the centre to the far wall.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "4", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50013", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">13/35</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2/5</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">13/14</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">37/105</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A committee of 4 members is to be selected at random from 6 men and 4 women. What is the probability that a particular man, Raghav, is on the committee and the committee has at least one woman?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Total ways.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Choose 4 from 10: ¹⁰C₄ = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">210</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Raghav is fixed in the committee.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The other 3 members come from the remaining </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> people (5 men, 4 women).</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Ways = ⁹C₃ = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">84</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Remove the committees with no woman.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">All 3 others are men: ⁵C₃ = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">10</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Favourable = 84 − 10 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">74</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image015.png\" width=\"80\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image016.png\" width=\"125\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image017.png\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Multiplying P(Raghav) = 2/5 by P(at least one woman) = 13/14 gives 13/35 — wrong, because once Raghav is in, only 3 seats are left and the two events are not independent.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "3", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50014", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9 : 10</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5 : 3</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">10 : 9</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">20 : 9</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A sector of a circle of radius 14 cm has a central angle of 150°. A sector of another circle of radius 21 cm has a central angle of π/3 radians. What is the ratio of the area of the first sector to the area of the second sector?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:3pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image018.png\" width=\"336\" height=\"141\" alt ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — area of a sector = (θ/360°) × πr², so the area varies as θ × r².</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Put both angles in degrees.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">π radians = 180°, so π/3 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">60°</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Ratio of θ × r².</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">First : second = 150 × 14² : 60 × 21²</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">= 150 × 196 : 60 × 441</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Cancel.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">150 : 60 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5 : 2</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">196 : 441 = 14² : 21² = 2² : 3² = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">4 : 9</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Ratio = 5 × 4 : 2 × 9 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">20 : 18 = 10 : 9</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">10 : 9</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Taking the radii as 14 : 21 instead of their squares gives 5 : 3 — area always goes with r².</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2025 Tier-I (13 Sep 2025, Shift 3)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "1", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50015", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3)(x − 3)(x − 2)(x² − 3x + 9)</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3)(x − 3)(x + 2)(x² − 3x + 9)</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3)²(x − 3)(x − 2)(x² − 3x + 9)</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x − 3)(x − 2)(x² + 3x + 9)</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">What is the LCM of x³ + 27, x² − 9 and x² + x − 6?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — factorise each expression; the LCM takes every factor once, at its highest power.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Factorise.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">x³ + 27 = x³ + 3³ = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3)(x² − 3x + 9)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">x² − 9 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3)(x − 3)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">x² + x − 6 = x² + 3x − 2x − 6 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3)(x − 2)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Collect the factors.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3) appears in all three, but only to the power </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The others: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x − 3)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x − 2)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x² − 3x + 9)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">LCM.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">LCM = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3)(x − 3)(x − 2)(x² − 3x + 9)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(x + 3)(x − 3)(x − 2)(x² − 3x + 9)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) — the middle sign is minus; (x² + 3x + 9) belongs to x³ − 27.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2022 Mains (Tier-II)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "2", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50016", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">x = 3</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">y = 2</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">y = 3</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">y = −2</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A straight line parallel to the x-axis passes through the point of intersection of the lines 2x + 3y = 12 and x − y = 1. What is the equation of this line?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:3pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image019.png\" width=\"240\" height=\"203\" alt ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — a line parallel to the x-axis is horizontal: every point on it has the same y, so its equation is y = k.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">k is the y-coordinate of the point it passes through.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Solve the two lines together.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">From x − y = 1: x = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">y + 1</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Put in 2x + 3y = 12:</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2(y + 1) + 3y = 12</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5y = 10 ⇒ y = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">x = 2 + 1 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Point of intersection = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(3, 2)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The horizontal line through (3, 2).</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">y = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">y = 2</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">x = 3 is the line through the same point parallel to the y-axis — 'parallel to the x-axis' fixes y, not x.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC Selection Post Phase XIV (Higher Secondary Level, 17 Sep 2026)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "1", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50017", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">0.69375</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">0.78125</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">0.27375</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">0.70375</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">What is the decimal form of </span><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image020.png\" width=\"133\" height=\"32\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> </span><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">simplify the fractions completely first, then convert once at the end.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;text-align:justify;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image021.png\" width=\"85\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;text-align:justify;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image022.png\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;text-align:justify;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image023.png\" width=\"289\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;text-align:justify;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image024.png\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;text-align:justify;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image025.png\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;text-align:justify;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image026.png\" width=\"176\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;text-align:justify;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image027.png\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;text-align:justify;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image028.png\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Convert to a decimal.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">160 = 2⁵ × 5, so the decimal terminates.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image029.png\" width=\"346\" height=\"40\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">0.69375</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Multiplying by 17/25 instead of dividing gives 289/800 and ends at 0.27375 — division by a fraction always flips it first.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2025 Tier-I (16 Sep 2025, Shift 3)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "4", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50018", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹24,500</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹26,000</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹28,000</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹25,000</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The compound interest on a sum of money for 3 years, at 10% per annum for the first year, 12% per annum for the second year and 15% per annum for the third year (compounded annually), is ₹10,420. What is the sum?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image030.png\" width=\"449\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image031.png\" width=\"344\" height=\"35\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image032.png\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image033.png\" width=\"155\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image034.png\" width=\"174\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image035.png\" width=\"252\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image036.png\" width=\"266\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image037.png\" width=\"40\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image038.png\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image039.png\" width=\"246\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹25,000</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The ₹10,420 is the interest, not the amount — subtract 1 from the factor before dividing.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC Selection Post Phase XIV (Graduate Level, 17 Sep 2026)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "3", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50019", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">162.5 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">161.5 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">160.5 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">160 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Study the histogram and answer the question.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image040.png\" width=\"365\" height=\"189\" alt ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The histogram above shows the heights (in cm) of 60 players of a sports academy. What is the median height of the players?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — median of grouped data = L + [(N/2 − cf) ÷ f] × h.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">L = lower limit of the median class, cf = cumulative frequency before it, f = its frequency, h = class width.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Read the frequencies and accumulate.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">145–150: 5 → cf </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">150–155: 9 → cf </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">14</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">155–160: 14 → cf </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">28</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">160–165: 20 → cf </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">48</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">165–170: 8 → cf 56</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">170–175: 4 → cf 60</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Locate the median class.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">N/2 = 60 ÷ 2 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">30</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The cumulative frequency first passes 30 in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">160–165</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">L = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">160</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, cf = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">28</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, f = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">20</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, h = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Substitute.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Median = 160 + [(30 − 28) ÷ 20] × 5</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">= 160 + 0.5 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">160.5 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">160.5 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">cf is the total up to the class BEFORE the median class (28), not up to the median class itself (48).</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "2", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50020", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">180</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">187.5</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">200</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">175</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">If 18% of a number is 27 less than 27% of the same number, what is 62½% of the number?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Turn the given difference into a single percentage.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">27% − 18% = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9%</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> of the number</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9% of N = 27</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Find the number.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image041.png\" width=\"166\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image042.png\" width=\"155\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image043.png\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image044.png\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Short trick.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1% = 27 ÷ 9 = 3, so 62.5% = 62.5 × 3 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">187.5</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">187.5</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">62½% is the fraction 5/8 — learning the eighths (12½%, 37½%, 62½%, 87½%) saves a step every time.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CHSL 2025 Tier-I (25 Nov 2025, Shift 2)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}]}